---
description: Documentation discipline — ADRs, module guides, READMEs, CHANGELOG, CLAUDE.md, MDC rules.
globs: ["docs/**/*.md", "**/CLAUDE.md", "**/README.md", "AGENTS.md", "CHANGELOG.md", "mkdocs.yml", ".cursor/rules/**/*.mdc"]
alwaysApply: false
---

- Architectural decisions go into `docs/architecture/adr/NNNN-short-slug.md`. Numbered sequentially,
  **immutable once merged** — supersede via a new ADR that links back to the old one.
- ADR template: **Context → Decision → Consequences**. Keep under ~200 lines.
- Every module has a `docs/modules/<name>.md` kept in sync with its public API — update it in the
  same PR as the API change. Module `README.md` files describe the module in product terms and
  **ship inside the wheel**, so they must stay present-tense and true.
- `CHANGELOG.md` gets an entry under `## [Unreleased]` for every user-visible change (Keep a
  Changelog format, newest first).
- **Never write status hedges or scaffolding into a long-lived file**: no "implementation pending",
  no "coming soon", no phase / sub-phase / step numbers, no links to a roadmap. There is no roadmap
  document in this repository and none is planned; describe what the code does today.
- **Link policy.** `docs/` is the MkDocs `docs_dir`, so a relative path that climbs above it does not
  resolve on the rendered site. Links between files **inside** `docs/` are relative `.md` links;
  links to anything **outside** `docs/` (`src/`, `examples/`, `tests/`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`,
  `CLAUDE.md`) are absolute
  `https://github.com/GemovicNemanja/strata-forge/blob/main/...` URLs. Adding or renaming a page
  under `docs/` means updating the `mkdocs.yml` nav; `make docs-build` runs `--strict` and fails on a
  broken link.
- Every code snippet must use symbols that actually exist — verify against `src/strata_forge` before
  writing an import or a call. Async examples need `asyncio.run` or an `await` context. A snippet
  that does not run is worse than no snippet.
- Install hints name the real distribution: `pip install 'strata-forge[<extra>]'`. `ai-forge` is a
  different project on PyPI.
- No emojis in documentation — headings, tables, or prose. The badges at the top of the root
  `README.md` are the only exception.
- The root `CLAUDE.md` is authoritative for cross-cutting rules; module-level `CLAUDE.md` files are
  authoritative for module-specific rules. **When a module rule conflicts with root, fix the
  conflict** before merging. `docs/agent-guide.md` is the how-to companion — navigation, task
  recipes, the verification loop — and must not restate the rules.
- `AGENTS.md` is a symlink to `CLAUDE.md` — do not turn it into a separate file.
- `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` files mirror specific sections of `CLAUDE.md` with `globs:` for scoped
  activation. Keep them brief and defer to `CLAUDE.md` for the full rationale.
- See `CLAUDE.md` §7 for the self-maintenance protocol — when a rule drifts from code, fix it in the
  same PR. Merged code wins over a stale rule; the rule file wins over in-flight code.
